{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Templating in DotKernel3{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">Dotkernel</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">Templating in DotKernel3</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="container py-4">
        <div class="row g-4">
            
            {% include '@partial/left-menu.html.twig' %}

            <main class="col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-9">
                <article class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5 h-100">
                    <header class="mb-4">
                        <h1 class="h2 text-dark fw-bold">Templating in DotKernel3</h1>
                        <div class="text-muted small">
                            <i class="bi bi-folder2-open me-1"></i> Dotkernel
                        </div>
                    </header>

                    <section class="post-content text-secondary lh-lg fs-6">
                        <strong>DotKernel3</strong> aims to improve the DotKernel stack in every way possible, and one of the painpoints in the previous version of DotKernel was the templating engine.
Albeit a solid and robust templating engine, it was also 10 years old, and used techniques that's slightly outdated by now.

In DotKernel 3, we made the move to the popular <a href="https://twig.symfony.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>Twig Templating Engine</strong></a>, which will allow us to take our templates to a whole new level. It can now be written as HTML code, with some extra Twig tags; It is incredibly powerful and includes features such as:

<ul>
<li>Layouts</li>
<li>Loops</li>
<li>Variables</li>
<li>Escaping</li>
</ul>

The templating engine in <strong>DotKernel3</strong> gives you the familiarity of HTML with the overview and convenience of PHP.

You can read the official documentation here: <a href="https://docs.dotkernel.com/Prerequisites/Templates" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>Templates</strong></a>
                    </section>
                </article>
            </main>
            
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}